.TH MYTOOTH 1 "September 2026" "Mytooth 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
mytooth \- Bluetooth manager for Cinnamon Wayland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mytooth
.RB [ --background ]
.RB [ --debug ]
.RB [ --quit ]
.RB [ --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Mytooth manages BlueZ adapters, discovery, pairing, devices and battery information.
It runs as the logged-in user and requires GTK 3, libxapp, BlueZ and a native Wayland session.
Closing the window retains the tray and pairing agent when a native XApp tray host is available.
Quit ends Mytooth without powering off adapters or disconnecting devices.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --background
Start with the window hidden. If no native XApp tray host appears, show the window.
.TP
.B --debug
Enable diagnostic logging for this process. Pairing secrets are not logged.
.TP
.B --quit
Quit the running instance.
.TP
.B --version
Print the application version.
.SH FILES
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mytooth/settings.ini
(normally ~/.config/mytooth/settings.ini) stores window size and notification preferences.
.PP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/autostart/io.github.the_specter_x.Mytooth.desktop
stores the optional login startup entry.
.SH LOGGING
When stderr is a terminal, logs are written there. Otherwise logs go to the
systemd journal, with stderr as fallback when journald is unavailable.
Read them with:
.PP
.B journalctl -t mytooth -b
.PP
The journal controls retention and storage, normally /var/log/journal for
persistent storage or /run/log/journal for volatile storage. Mytooth does not
write or rotate its own log files and does not require root privileges.
.SH NOTES
Incoming requests require Mytooth to be the default BlueZ agent. Pairing is
paused while Cinnamon reports an active screensaver, or its status is unknown.
Avoid running another Bluetooth pairing agent at the same time.
